      "side": 1,
      "message": "Unfortunately this doesn\u0027t fix the issue, it only makes it less likely, because onLost can still be called between block() and the read of the member, and reset it to null.\n\nOne thing you could do is the following :\n\n  while (true) {\n    val n \u003d currentNetwork;\n    if (n !\u003d null) return n;\n    mAvailableCv.block();\n  }\n\n...however I\u0027m not sure it helps very much, because while it guarantees to return non-null, it doesn\u0027t guarantee the network won\u0027t disconnect milliseconds later and the user won\u0027t get the wrong network object.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 717,
        "startChar": 32,
        "endLine": 717,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "e34b9758601c20c53e87ed82dd5c2b37d996d273",
